30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems a high upfront cost scares off potential members, and tiered grades caused friction in the past.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The paperwork for mid-year joiners is a mess, and chasing small payments is eating up the treasurer's time.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,A tiny fraction of us are doing all the attending and all the work. It's incredibly uneven.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Charging for outings seems to have killed the momentum for weekday meetings. People feel less ownership.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Most of our costs are fixed regardless of attendance, and getting people to pay on time is a struggle.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if the costs are mostly fixed, does that mean we have a minimum we must collect?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, if only a few people are doing the work, a flat fee might feel like a subsidy for the inactive.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,Exactly. The people carrying the club are the ones who would be most annoyed by an unfair system.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, if people are hesitant to join or attend, we can't make the barrier to entry any higher.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"Yes, Asuka, seventy percent is fixed. We can't afford to let the budget slide based on turnout.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, but if chasing small payments is the problem, then activity-based charging sounds like a nightmare.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,It absolutely is. Six hours a month just chasing session money is unsustainable for a volunteer.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We need a system that acknowledges the heavy users without punishing the casual ones too harshly.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,But we also can't have people weighing up every single evening they attend. It kills the community.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Takumi,,And we can't ignore that some people need to spread their payments out.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
