55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is simple, but the taster forms show people hate a big upfront commitment.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is a treasurer's nightmare. I strongly lean toward Option A for the sake of sanity.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option B might address the unevenness, but Asuka mentioned it caused friction previously.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is out for me; it makes every visit a transaction and discourages the regulars.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A is the only way to ensure our fixed costs are covered without guesswork.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if we go with A, can we offer a payment plan to help those who struggle?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,That's still easier than chasing a dozen small fees every week. I vote for A.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If B is too divisive, then A is the most stable, even if it feels slightly unfair to the casuals.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,I agree. We need to stop people from calculating the cost of every single evening. I vote A.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Takumi,,A payment plan is manageable. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I'm torn, but B seems too risky for the social health. I'll vote for A.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I'll vote for A as well. It's the cleanest solution for the books.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
